  "title": "B.L.",
  "summary": "Bree is frantic and apologetic. June asked her questions about the count before she died, and Bree needs \"till the weekend\" to be sure of something before she says more. Tess can't tell whether she's guilty or scared. Paul gets in touch, cheerful and \"nothing to hide\". He steers Tess toward Bree's hard year, asks whether the police have traced the number, and offers June's delivery log for the estate.",
